course: dictionary
lesson: 6108
title: Mica, the sparkly mineral
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rock is made of minerals, and each mineral is a natural solid. Mica is one of these minerals. You can find it inside rocks such as granite. Scientists read the words around a new word to learn what it means, and you can do the same.
explain: «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica, formed deep underground.» The sentence tells you that mica is one of the crystals inside granite, so it is a part of the rock, not a separate rock.
explain: «Granite is a mix of grains of quartz, feldspar and mica that you can see with a magnifying glass.» Mica is a mineral, and its shiny flakes catch the light. Look for the words sheets and flakes, because they tell you what mica looks like.
fact: Mica is a mineral, which means a natural solid material.
fact: Mica splits into very thin, shiny, see-through sheets.
fact: «Mica» is the sparkly part of granite, seen as glittery flakes.
fact: Mica does not burn easily, so it is used in some make-up, paints and electrical parts.
fact: Rocks are made of minerals, and granite is a mix of quartz, feldspar and mica.
exercise: «Granite is a speckled rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica.» What kind of thing is mica here? | A type of water | *A mineral found in the rock | A kind of plant | A rock that floats on water
exercise: Mica splits into very thin sheets. Which words describe these sheets? | Soft and sticky | Thick and heavy | Dull and black | *Thin and shiny
exercise: According to the lesson, what are rocks made of? | Water and air | Sand only | Plastic | *Minerals
test: «Granite is a mix of grains of quartz, feldspar and mica that you can see with a magnifying glass.» What helps you see the mica grains? | *A magnifying glass | A torch | A telescope | A mirror
test: Mica is used in some electrical parts. Why? | It floats on water | *It does not burn easily | It tastes sweet | It is heavy
exam: Which phrase uses mica correctly? | a mica of tea | *sheets of mica | mica bread | cups of mica
